Pyre vendored copy of the Termux terminal libraries
====================================================

Source: https://github.com/termux/termux-app, tag v0.118.3
        (commit in UPSTREAM-COMMIT), modules terminal-emulator and
        terminal-view.

Licence: Apache License 2.0 (text in LICENSE). The termux-app repository is
GPLv3 overall; its LICENSE.md (copied verbatim as UPSTREAM-LICENSE.md) states
that the terminal-view and terminal-emulator libraries are an exception,
released under the Apache License 2.0 because they derive from Jack Palevich's
"Terminal Emulator for Android" (https://github.com/jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator,
Apache-2.0). Upstream ships no per-module LICENSE/NOTICE file; no other Termux
code (app/, termux-shared/, the GPLv3 parts) is included.

Copyright (C) 2011-2016 Steven Luo, Jack Palevich and contributors (Terminal
Emulator for Android); Copyright the Termux developers.

Modifications by Pyre (2026-10):
- com/termux/terminal/TerminalSession.java rewritten as a remote session: the
  JNI/forkpty subprocess, its threads and the native library were removed;
  bytes from the Pyre web-terminal relay are fed via feed(), keyboard input and
  resizes are sent through TerminalSession.RemoteIo. Public API used by
  TerminalView is unchanged.
- com/termux/terminal/JNI.java and src/main/jni (native termux.c) removed.
- Build converted to a Gradle Kotlin DSL Android library module.
All other files are unmodified upstream sources.
